Below is a minimal patch which makes the “constructor-super” rule defensive against un-initialized segments.  The core of the bug is that, under some control-flow constructs (e.g. `try/catch` + `for…of`), `onCodePathSegmentStart` never fires for *every* segment, so later calls to

```js
segInfoMap[segment.id].superCalled
```

will blow up when `segInfoMap[segment.id]` is `undefined`.  We simply guard that lookup.  

